{
  "requirement": "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed\ncheck it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.\nThis is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check\nstates which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as\na malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:\nits error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and\nchecks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.\n\nThe code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.\nA repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them\nin a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a\nvariable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is\nnot one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check\nthat does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the\nsame loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.\n\n::::{sites} error_accumulators\n```yaml\nlanguage: rust\npaths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]\nexclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]\nrule:\n  kind: function_item\n  has:\n    stopBy: { kind: function_item }\n    any:\n      - kind: parameter\n        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }\n      - kind: let_declaration\n        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }\n  not:\n    inside:\n      stopBy: end\n      kind: mod_item\n      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }\nmatch:\n  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"\n  - |\n    fn run() {\n        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();\n        check(\"\", &mut errors);\n    }\nno_match:\n  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"\n  - |\n    fn run() {\n        let mut problems = Vec::new();\n        check(\"\", &mut problems);\n    }\n  - |\n    mod tests {\n        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\n    }\n```\n::::\n\n::::{violations} early_exits\n```yaml\nlanguage: rust\npaths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]\nwithin: error_accumulators\nrule:\n  any:\n    - kind: try_expression\n    - kind: return_expression\n    - kind: continue_expression\n    - kind: break_expression\nmatch:\n  - |\n    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {\n        let n = v.as_u64()?;\n        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }\n        Some(n as u8)\n    }\n  - |\n    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {\n        for item in items {\n            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }\n            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }\n        }\n    }\n  - |\n    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {\n        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }\n        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }\n    }\n  - |\n    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {\n        for item in items {\n            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }\n        }\n        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }\n    }\nno_match:\n  - |\n    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {\n        let n = v.as_u64()?;\n        Some(n as u8)\n    }\n```\n::::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations and tests**\n\n- **Continue after a failed check and report every failure in one run.** These tests assert many distinct errors from one run:\n  - `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors]`\n  - `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failed_checks_do_not_hide_later_independent_checks]`\n  - `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[schema_rejects_each_malformed_field_and_input_form]`\n  - `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[inspection_progress_preserves_validation_and_finishes_each_phase]`\n  - `tests/references.rs#fn[malformed_citation_entries_do_not_hide_later_independent_errors]`\n  - `tests/references.rs#fn[unclosed_fences_still_report_unknown_names]`\n  - `src/execution_coverage/check.rs#mod[tests]/fn[accepted_exceptions_cannot_waive_invalid_measurement_and_checks_still_collect_errors]`\n- **An unparseable file is one failed check, and independent checks still run.**\n  - Broken `habeas.toml`, `book.toml` and evidence JSON are covered by `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks]`.\n  - They are also covered by `tests/commands.rs#fn[status_loads_nearest_workspace_file_without_validating_authoring]`.\n  - Coverage and nextest configuration failures are covered in the same test.\n  - A failed Git index read is covered by `git_index_failure_is_reported_once_and_later_checks_still_run`.\n  - The tests assert that the expected later errors still appear.\n  - They also assert the configuration errors appear exactly once.\n  - The \"MAY report only the first problem\" clause imposes nothing to test.\n- **MUST NOT report one failure twice.**\n  - The tests assert unique error lists, or exact counts, in several places:\n    - `failed_checks_do_not_hide_later_independent_checks`\n    - the coverage-measurement test\n    - the git-index test\n    - `src/index.rs#mod[tests]/fn[an_unreadable_record_is_reported_once]`\n    - `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs#fn[an_unlistable_review_directory_is_reported_once]`\n    - `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failed_site_queries_do_not_repeat_errors_through_dependent_violations]`\n    - `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[every_review_kind_loads_both_formats_and_reports_each_application_failure_once]`\n  - Site-query failures are covered by `a_violation_query_needs_a_site_query` and `within_cannot_name_another_violation_query`.\n- **Naming an error accumulator `errors`, and sites running later checks.** These are upheld by each site and covered by the site reviews. They need no test here.\n\n**Site query `error_accumulators`.** I ran it. It returns the validation functions that take an `errors: &mut Vec<String>` or `BTreeSet<String>` parameter, or hold a local `errors`. Examples are `inspect_repository_with_progress`, `validate_evidence_file`, `citations::validate`, `sites::discover`, `check_saved` and `github::check_reviewed_issues`.\n\nI searched `src` for other accumulator names. The aborting collectors named `failures` are not validation sites:\n- `delete_orphaned_reviews`\n- `load_definition_snapshots`\n- `reference_set_digest_for`\n\nThe other names are not validation either. `rewrite_record` is a refactoring helper, `notes::pages` renders documentation, and `status_markdown_with_github` builds report text. I found no validation function that holds its errors under another name.\n\nThe exclusions of `src/authoring/inputs.rs` and `src/authoring/tools.rs`, and of `mod tests`, match the stated scope.\n\n**Snippets.**\n- The site query has match snippets for the parameter and `let` forms.\n- It has no_match snippets for a different name, a different local name, and a `tests` module.\n- The violation query has match snippets for `?`, `continue`, `return` and `break`.\n- It has a no_match snippet for a function with no `errors` variable.\n\nThis is adequate. The violation query's `within: error_accumulators` is exercised.\n\nI found no adequacy gaps.",
